```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <title>Video Slider</title>
 <style>
 body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 0; background-color: #f4f4f9; }
 .slider-container { width: 100%; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); }
 .video-slider { display: flex; transition: transform 0.5s ease; }
 .video-slide { min-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
 .video-wrapper { position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
 .video-wrapper iframe { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
 .controls { text-align: center; margin: 20px 0; }
 .control-btn { padding: 10px 20px; background-color: #007bff; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; margin: 0 10px; transition: background-color 0.3s ease; }
 .control-btn:hover { background-color: #0056b3; }
 </style>
</head>
<body>

 <div class="slider-container">
 <div class="video-slider">
 <div class="video-slide">
 <div class="video-wrapper">
 <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/videoid1" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div class="video-slide">
 <div class="video-wrapper">
 <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/videoid2" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>
 </div>
 </div>
 <!-- Add more video slides as needed -->
 </div>
 </div>

 <div class="controls">
 <button class="control-btn" onclick="prevSlide()">Previous</button>
 <button class="control-btn" onclick="nextSlide()">Next</button>
 </div>

 <script>
 let currentSlide = 0;
 const slides = document.querySelector('.video-slider');
 const totalSlides = document.querySelectorAll('.video-slide').length;

 function showSlide(index) {
 slides.style.transform = `translateX(-${index * 100}%)`;
 }

 function prevSlide() {
 currentSlide = (currentSlide > 0) ? currentSlide - 1 : totalSlides - 1;
 showSlide(currentSlide);
 }

 function nextSlide() {
 currentSlide = (currentSlide < totalSlides - 1) ? currentSlide + 1 : 0;
 showSlide(currentSlide);
 }
 </script>

</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**
- The slider utilizes a flexbox container to align the video slides horizontally.
- Each video is wrapped in a responsive container for maintaining aspect ratio.
- CSS transitions ensure smooth sliding animations.
- JavaScript functions control the slide transitions allowing you to navigate through videos.

