Certainly! Creating accessible modal dialogs involves focusing on keyboard navigation and screen reader compatibility. Here's a simple HTML/CSS snippet that demonstrates a keyboard-friendly and accessible modal dialog:

```html
<!-- Modal HTML Structure -->
<div class="modal" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="modalTitle" aria-hidden="true">
 <div class="modal-overlay" tabindex="-1"></div>
 <div class="modal-content" role="document">
 <header class="modal-header">
 <h2 id="modalTitle" class="modal-title">Welcome to Our Site</h2>
 <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close modal" onclick="closeModal()">&times;</button>
 </header>
 <div class="modal-body">
 <p>To navigate this site effectively, please follow our accessibility guidelines.</p>
 </div>
 <footer class="modal-footer">
 <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="acceptModal()">Accept</button>
 <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="closeModal()">Cancel</button>
 </footer>
 </div>
</div>

<!-- CSS for Styling -->
<style>
.modal {
 display: none; /* Hidden by default */
 position: fixed;
 top: 0;
 left: 0;
 width: 100%;
 height: 100%;
 background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
 z-index: 1000;
 justify-content: center;
 align-items: center;
}
.modal-content {
 background-color: #fff;
 padding: 20px;
 border-radius: 5px;
 width: 80%;
 max-width: 500px;
 outline: none;
}
.modal-title {
 margin: 0;
}
.modal-close {
 background: transparent;
 border: none;
 font-size: 1.5rem;
 position: absolute;
 top: 10px;
 right: 10px;
 cursor: pointer;
}
</style>

<!-- JavaScript to Handle Modal -->
<script>
function openModal() {
 const modal = document.querySelector('.modal');
 modal.style.display = 'flex';
 modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
 modal.querySelector('.modal-content').focus();
}

function closeModal() {
 const modal = document.querySelector('.modal');
 modal.style.display = 'none';
 modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
}

function acceptModal() {
 // Implement accept action
 closeModal();
}

// Event listeners for accessibility
window.addEventListener('keydown', function(event) {
 const modal = document.querySelector('.modal');
 if (modal.style.display === 'flex' && event.key === 'Escape') {
 closeModal();
 }
});
</script>
```

**Key Features:**
 - **Keyboard Navigation**: Users can open and close the modal using keyboard shortcuts. The `Escape` key closes the modal.
 - **ARIA Attributes**: Provides semantic meaning for screen readers through `aria-labelledby` and `aria-hidden`.
 - **Focus Management**: Ensures that the modal content is focused when opened, enhancing user experience.

