 <style>
 .tooltip-container {
 position: relative;
 display: inline-block;
 cursor: pointer;
 }

 .tooltip-text {
 visibility: hidden;
 width: 120px;
 background-color: #555;
 color: #fff;
 text-align: center;
 border-radius: 4px;
 padding: 5px 0;
 position: absolute;
 z-index: 1;
 bottom: 125%;
 left: 50%;
 margin-left: -60px;
 opacity: 0;
 transition: opacity 0.3s;
 }

 .tooltip-container:hover .tooltip-text {
 visibility: visible;
 opacity: 1;
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="tooltip-container">
 Hover over me
 <span class="tooltip-text">Tooltip text</span>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**
- The `.tooltip-container` class is used to define the element that will trigger the tooltip on hover.
- The `.tooltip-text` class styles the tooltip itself. It is initially hidden using `visibility: hidden` and `opacity: 0`. When you hover over the container, these properties change to make the tooltip visible.
- The tooltip is positioned relative to the container, and CSS transitions are used to animate its appearance gracefully.

Feel free to customize the styles and positioning as needed for your website's design.

