<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <title>Accessible FAQ</title>
 <style>
 .faq {
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 max-width: 800px;
 margin: 0 auto;
 padding: 20px;
 }

 .faq-question {
 font-weight: bold;
 margin-bottom: 10px;
 }

 .faq-answer {
 margin-bottom: 20px;
 display: none;
 }

 .faq-toggle:focus {
 outline: 2px solid #ffcc00;
 }
 </style>
 <script>
 function toggleAnswer(event) {
 const answer = event.target.nextElementSibling;
 if (answer.style.display === "none" || answer.style.display === "") {
 answer.style.display = "block";
 } else {
 answer.style.display = "none";
 }
 }
 </script>
</head>
<body>
 <div class="faq">
 <button class="faq-toggle" onclick="toggleAnswer(event)">What is HTML?</button>
 <div class="faq-answer">
 <p>HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language and is the standard language for creating web pages.</p>
 </div>

 <button class="faq-toggle" onclick="toggleAnswer(event)">Why is accessibility important?</button>
 <div class="faq-answer">
 <p>Accessibility ensures that all users, including those with disabilities, can access and use web content effectively.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
</body>
</html>
```

### Key Accessibility Features:
- **Keyboard Accessibility:** Interactive elements (buttons) are focusable using the Tab key, allowing keyboard users to navigate through questions.
- **Focus Indication:** Visual feedback on focused elements using the `:focus` pseudo-class.
- **Semantic HTML:** Usage of semantic tags for better understanding by screen readers.

