```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <style>
 .accordion {
 background-color: #f1f1f1;
 border: 1px solid #ccc;
 border-radius: 5px;
 max-width: 600px;
 margin: auto;
 padding: 10px;
 }
 .accordion-item {
 margin-bottom: 10px;
 }
 .accordion-header {
 font-size: 1.2em;
 cursor: pointer;
 padding: 10px;
 border-radius: 5px;
 background-color: #007BFF;
 color: white;
 }
 .accordion-content {
 display: none;
 padding: 10px;
 background: #fff;
 border-radius: 5px;
 }
 </style>
 <script>
 function toggleAccordion(event) {
 const content = event.currentTarget.nextElementSibling;
 if (content.style.display === "block") {
 content.style.display = "none";
 } else {
 content.style.display = "block";
 }
 }
 document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
 const headers = document.querySelectorAll('.accordion-header');
 headers.forEach(header => {
 header.addEventListener('click', toggleAccordion);
 });
 });
 </script>
</head>
<body>
 <div class="accordion">
 <div class="accordion-item">
 <div class="accordion-header">Section 1</div>
 <div class="accordion-content">Content for section 1. Loaded dynamically with JavaScript.</div>
 </div>
 <div class="accordion-item">
 <div class="accordion-header">Section 2</div>
 <div class="accordion-content">Content for section 2. Loaded dynamically with JavaScript.</div>
 </div>
 </div>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **Accordion Structure**: The accordion consists of header items that act as toggles for showing and hiding content.
- **Dynamic Loading**: JavaScript is used to toggle the display of the content when a header is clicked.
- **Accessibility Enhancements**: Consider adding ARIA roles to make the accordion more accessible for screen readers.

