Absolutely! Accessible accordions are a great way to enhance user experience for all, including those using assistive technologies. Here is a simple example of an accessible accordion:

```html
<section class="accordion">
 <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
 <div class="accordion-item">
 <button class="accordion-button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="panel1" id="accordion1">
 What is an accordion in UI design?
 </button>
 <div class="accordion-panel" id="panel1" role="region" aria-labelledby="accordion1" hidden>
 <p>An accordion is a vertically stacked list of items that allows users to toggle the display of sections of content.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div class="accordion-item">
 <button class="accordion-button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="panel2" id="accordion2">
 How do you make an accordion accessible?
 </button>
 <div class="accordion-panel" id="panel2" role="region" aria-labelledby="accordion2" hidden>
 <p>To make an accordion accessible, use semantic HTML, manage focus, and ensure ARIA attributes are correctly applied.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

<style>
 .accordion {
 border: 1px solid #ddd;
 padding: 10px;
 border-radius: 5px;
 }
 .accordion-button {
 background: none;
 border: none;
 text-align: left;
 width: 100%;
 padding: 15px;
 font-size: 1rem;
 cursor: pointer;
 outline: none;
 }
 .accordion-panel {
 padding: 0 15px;
 max-height: 0;
 overflow: hidden;
 transition: max-height 0.2s ease-out;
 }
 .accordion-button[aria-expanded="true"] + .accordion-panel {
 max-height: 100px;
 }
</style>

<script>
 document.querySelectorAll('.accordion-button').forEach(button => {
 button.addEventListener('click', function() {
 const panel = this.nextElementSibling;
 const expanded = this.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true' || false;

 this.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !expanded);
 panel.hidden = expanded;
 });
 });
</script>
```

**Explanation:**
- **Semantic HTML:** Using `<button>` and `<div>` tags with appropriate ARIA attributes to describe the roles and relationships of each element.
- **ARIA Attributes:** `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, and `aria-labelledby` help in describing the state and the relationship between buttons and panels.
- **Focus Management:** JavaScript ensures that when the button is clicked, the corresponding panel's visibility is toggled.

